course: dictionary
lesson: 14909
title: Reddened: when something turns red
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Reddened» is the past form of «redden», which means to become red or to make something red. Read the words around it: «Mia's cheeks reddened when the whole class laughed at her spelling.» Her face changed colour, so reddened must mean went red.
explain: Ask why it happened. She was embarrassed, which means shy and awkward. Anger can make a face go red too: «Dad's face reddened with anger when the vase broke.»
explain: Reddened can describe skin or eyes. «After a day at the beach, his shoulders reddened in the sun.» That is sunburn. «Her reddened eyes showed she had been crying.» Here reddened describes the eyes, so it is an adjective.
explain: Use the swap test. Put «went red» into the sentence in place of reddened. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Reddened is the past form of redden, and it means became red or made something red.
fact: «Reddened» can mean went red in the face from shame, anger or embarrassment. This is called blushing.
fact: «Reddened» can also be an adjective describing something red and often sore, such as «reddened eyes».
fact: Skin reddens in the sun, which is a sign of sunburn, so cover up and use cream.
fact: The sky reddens at sunset, when the sun goes down and the light turns red and orange.
exercise: «Her cheeks reddened when everyone turned to look at her.» What does reddened mean? | *Went red in the face from embarrassment | Became cold and pale | Grew taller | Fell asleep
exercise: «The sky reddened as the sun went down.» What does reddened mean here? | Fell down | *Became red | Got wet | Turned black and dark
exercise: «After a day at the beach, his shoulders were reddened, so he needs cream.» What does reddened suggest? | A new red shirt | A cold winter day | Happy laughter | *Skin turned red and sore from the sun
test: «Dad's face reddened with anger.» Which phrase means the same as reddened here? | Went quiet and calm | Fell over | *Went red with anger | Sang loudly
test: «Her reddened eyes showed she had been crying.» What kind of word is reddened in «reddened eyes»? | Verb | Adverb | *Adjective | Noun
exam: «Ben's ears reddened when the teacher asked him a question.» What is the best meaning for reddened? | Got bigger | *Went red with embarrassment | Went cold | Laughed loudly
